::Q1::What is Amazon EC2?
{
~An identity and access management service
=A service for running virtual servers in the cloud~An object storage service
~A managed relational database service
}

::Q2::Why does instance type selection affect cost? 
{
~All instance types have exactly the same price
~Instance type changes only the server's hostname
~Instance type determines the S3 storage class=Different instance types provide different amounts and types of resources at different prices
}

::Q3::What is one important configuration choice when launching an EC2 instance? 
{
=The instance type
~The Python package version only
~The SQL table name only
~The S3 object key only
}


::Q4::What is a practical way to reduce EC2 cost when a workload does not need the instance running? 
{
=Stop the instance when it is no longer needed, where appropriate
~Disable all network access permanently
~Increase the instance size
~Duplicate the instance   
}

::Q5::What does setting up a Python environment on EC2 allow a developer to do? 
{
~Create IAM policies without AWS
~Turn EC2 into an S3 bucket
~Convert the instance into a relational table
=Run Python-based workload or pipeline code on the instance
}